      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is `call_count\u003d\u003d2`?",
      "revId": "3f0a9982f1efe9195a571dcca4539f51936db5aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf2fa762_b07aa9e2",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/amd_power/src/amd_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T16:55:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have to toggle the GPIO twice.  So the code we\u0027re trying to detect looks like this: ```\n        /*\n         * Send a pulse to SYS_RST to trigger a warm reset.\n         */\n        gpio_set_level(GPIO_SYS_RESET_L, 0);\n        usleep(32 * MSEC);\n        gpio_set_level(GPIO_SYS_RESET_L, 1);\n```\n\nIf you have a suggestion past counting the edges, I can adjust the logic.",
      "parentUuid": "36a9c8c5_e5ec08f7",
      "revId": "3f0a9982f1efe9195a571dcca4539f51936db5aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "900b6d2b_b2c5ad19",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/amd_power/src/amd_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T17:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, that makes sense. Just wanted to make sure this isn\u0027t a fragile check, if this scenario changes.  Would `call_count !\u003d 0` be better?",
      "parentUuid": "bf2fa762_b07aa9e2",
      "revId": "3f0a9982f1efe9195a571dcca4539f51936db5aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "acdabe53_772838bd",
        "filename": "zephyr/test/amd_power/src/amd_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 515,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-05T17:18:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d be relatively surprised if the toggle changes since we\u0027ve been using it on the last 3 generations of processors.  So any change would need a new CONFIG or need to be tied into some other board-specific indicator, and that change could then update the unit test to ensure old boards still get the right toggle while new code uses the new toggle.",
      "parentUuid": "900b6d2b_b2c5ad19",
      "revId": "3f0a9982f1efe9195a571dcca4539f51936db5aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
